    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0470" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.01/31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-20T12:00:00-03:00">September 20,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 20—11:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>57. I am reliably informed that today Brazil “will enter into friendly relations”
                    with the Governments of Argentina and Bolivia.</p>
                <p>The attitude of the Peruvian Government towards ex-President Leguia and towards
                    persons who have sought asylum in the Brazilian Legation in Lima will probably
                    cause Brazil to postpone its recognition for a few days.<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d378-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d378-f1" n="10" xml:id="d378-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 58, September 20, 2 p.m., the Chargé in Brazil reported that he
                    had just been informed that Brazil would recognize the Government of Peru that
                    day; <ref target="frus1930v03#pg_759">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>,
                        p. 759</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
